020. \n\nNow, add the two results together: 335 and 4020. Let's add them step by step. 335 + 4000 is 4335, and then add the remaining 20 to get 4355. So, the product of 67 and 65 is 4355. \n\nWait, let me check that again to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe there's another way to verify. \n\nAlternatively, I can use the distributive property. Let's break down 65 into 60 + 5. So, 67 times 60 plus 67 times 5. \n\n67 times 60: 67 times 6 is 402, so times 10 is 4020. \n\n67 times 5: 67 times 5 is 335. \n\nAdding those together: 4020 + 335. Let's do that. 4020 + 300 is 4320, then +35 is 4355. Same result. Okay, that checks out. \n\nAnother way could be to use the formula (a + b)(a - b) = a² - b², but I don't think that applies here because 67 and 65 are not conjugates. Let me see. If I take a = 66 and b = 1, then (66 + 1)(66 - 1) = 66² - 1². But 66 squared is 4356, minus 1 is 4355. Oh, that's another way to get the same answer! So, that's a clever shortcut. \n\nSo, using that method, I also get 4355. That's reassuring. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the lattice method. Hmm, that might be more complicated, but let's try. \n\nFor 67 × 65, set up a lattice. \n\nFirst, write 67 and 65 as rows. \n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa067  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0×\xa0\xa065  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0------  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa05\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa035  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa060\xa0\xa0\xa0402  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0------\xa0\xa0\xa0------  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0335\xa0\xa0\xa04020  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0------\xa0\xa0\xa0------  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa04355  \n\nWait, that's the same as the standard multiplication method. So, yeah, same result. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use mental math. Let's see. 67 times 60 is 4020, and 67 times 5 is 335. Adding those gives 4355. Yep, same answer. \n\nI think all methods are leading me to 4355. Let me just verify with another check. Maybe using another multiplication technique. \n\nAlternatively, I can use the fact that 67