would be 1820, but since I subtracted 4 more than needed, I need to add 4 back. So 1820 + 4 is 1824. Okay, same result. That's a good sign.\n\nAnother way: Maybe break down 96 into 90 and 6. So, 90 times 19 plus 6 times 19. Let's calculate each part. 90 times 19. 90 times 10 is 900, 90 times 9 is 810. So 900 + 810 is 1710. Then 6 times 19. 6 times 10 is 60, 6 times 9 is 54. So 60 + 54 is 114. Then add 1710 and 114. 1710 + 100 is 1810, plus 14 is 1824. Again, same answer. So that's reassuring.\n\nWait, maybe I can use another method. Let's try using the lattice method. Hmm, not sure if I remember that correctly, but let's try. For 96 and 19, set up a grid. Multiply 96 by 1 and 96 by 9, then add them up. Wait, that's the same as the standard multiplication. Maybe not helpful here. Alternatively, maybe use the fact that 19 is a prime number? Not sure if that helps here. Maybe not necessary.\n\nAlternatively, use estimation. 96 is approximately 100, and 19 is approximately 20. So 100 times 20 is 2000. But since 96 is 4 less than 100 and 19 is 1 more than 18, maybe adjust accordingly. Hmm, this might not be the best approach. Let me think. The actual product is 1824, which is 2000 - 176. But this estimation is too rough. Maybe not helpful.\n\nAlternatively, use decimal multiplication. Let's write 96 as 96.0 and 19 as 19.0. Multiply them. \n\nFirst, multiply 96 by 19.0. Let's do it step by step. \n\nMultiply 96 by 9: 864. Then multiply 96 by 1 (tens place): 960. Add them together: 864 + 960 = 1824. Yep, same result. \n\nAlternatively, use the standard algorithm. \n\n     96\n   x 19\n   ------\n     864  (96 x 9)\n   960   (96 x 10, shifted one position to the left)\n   ------\n    1824\n\nYes, that's the same as before. So all methods are leading me to 1824. \n\nWait, maybe check with another multiplication technique. Like, using the 12 times table or something. Hmm, 19 is close to 20, so 19 x 96 = 20 x 96 - 96. Which is 1920 - 96 = 1824. That's the same as before. \n\nAlternatively, use the fact that 96 x 19 = 96 x (20 - 1) = 96 x 20 - 96 x 1 = 1920 - 96 = 1824. Yep, same answer. \n\nI think I've checked it multiple ways. All methods give 1824. So I can be confident that the product of 96 and 19 is 1824. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 96 and 19 is \\boxed{1824}.\n"]
