 find the product of 81 and 36, we can use multiple methods to verify the result:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Method:**\n   - Multiply 6 (units digit of 36) by 81: \\(6 \\times 81 = 486\\).\n   - Multiply 3 (tens digit of 36) by 81 and shift left by one position: \\(3 \\times 81 = 243\\) (becomes 2430).\n   - Add the partial products: \\(486 + 2430 = 2916\\).\n\n2. **Factoring Method:**\n   - Factor 81 as \\(9 \\times 9\\) and 36 as \\(4 \\times 9\\).\n   - Multiply the factors: \\((9 \\times 9) \\times (4 \\times 9) = 9 \\times 9 \\times 4 \\times 9\\).\n   - Calculate \\(9 \\times 9 \\times 4 \\times 9\\): \\(9 \\times 9 = 81\\), then \\(81 \\times 4 = 324\\), then \\(324 \\times 9 = 2916\\).\n\n3. **Distributive Property:**\n   - Break down 36 into 30 and 6: \\(81 \\times 36 = 81 \\times (30 + 6)\\).\n   - Calculate \\(81 \\times 30 = 2430\\) and \\(81 \\times 6 = 486\\).\n   - Add the results: \\(2430 + 486 = 2916\\).\n\n4. **Difference of Squares Method:**\n   - Express 81 as \\(9^2\\) and 36 as \\(6^2\\).\n   - Use the formula \\((a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2\\) where \\(a = 54\\) and \\(b = 0\\): \\(54^2 = 2916\\).\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 81 and 36 is \\(\\boxed{2916}\\).",
