et's compute that. 6241 - 70 is 6171, then subtract 9 more: 6171 - 9 = 6162. So that's the same result as before. So that's a quicker way. Instead of multiplying directly, using the difference of squares formula. That's clever.\n\nSo both methods give me 6162. Let me verify with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property again but in a different way.\n\n78 * 79 can be written as 70*79 + 8*79. Let's compute each part:\n\n70*79: 70*70 = 4900, 70*9 = 630. So 4900 + 630 = 5530.\n\n8*79: 8*70 = 560, 8*9 = 72. So 560 + 72 = 632.\n\nAdding those two results: 5530 + 632. Let's see, 5530 + 600 = 6130, then +32 = 6162. Again, same answer. Okay, so three different methods all leading to 6162. That gives me confidence that the answer is correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using a calculator to check. But since I don't have a calculator here, I'll just rely on my previous calculations. All three methods align, so I think 6162 is the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 78 and 79 is \\boxed{6162}.\n"]
