 calculations. \n\nAnother check: 15 times 50 is 750, subtract 15 gives 735. Correct. \n\nAlternatively, 49 times 10 is 490, 49 times 5 is 245. Then 490 + 245 is 735. Yep, that's another way. \n\nSo, all methods converge to 735. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 15 and 49 is indeed 735. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 15 and 49 is \\boxed{735}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 15 and 49, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Breaking down into tens and ones:**\n   - \\(15 = 10 + 5\\)\n   - \\(49 = 40 + 9\\)\n   - Calculate each part:\n     - \\(10 \\times 40 = 400\\)\n     - \\(10 \\times 9 = 90\\)\n     - \\(5 \\times 40 = 200\\)\n     - \\(5 \\times 9 = 45\\)\n   - Add the results: \\(400 + 90 + 200 + 45 = 735\\)\n\n2. **Standard multiplication method:**\n   - Multiply 15 by 9: \\(15 \\times 9 = 135\\)\n   - Multiply 15 by 40: \\(15 \\times 40 = 600\\)\n   - Add the results: \\(135 + 600 = 735\\)\n\n3. **Using the distributive property:**\n   - \\(15 \\times 49 = 15 \\times (50 - 1) = 15 \\times 50 - 15 \\times 1\\)\n   - Calculate each part: \\(15 \\times 50 = 750\\) and \\(15 \\times 1 = 15\\)\n   - Subtract the results: \\(750 - 15 = 735\\)\n\n4. **Adding 15 fifty times and subtracting 15:**\n   - \\(15 \\times 50 = 750\\)\n   - Subtract 15: \\(750 - 15 = 735\\)\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 15 and 49 is \\(\\boxed{735}\\).",
